			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>EngRunngDirSt1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Engine: Engine Running Direction State</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Engine running direction state.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Rotation direction of the combustion engine.
Used, for example, for engine stop/start systems.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Sign of the engine running direction:
If the vehicle is moving in the forward direction, and the drivetrain is closed, and a forward gear is engaged, then the engine running direction is positive.
During initialization, the engine sends the value "0".</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">0 = undefined running direction, no direction information available
1 = positive running direction
2 = negative running direction
3 = invalid running direction due to error</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>EngRunngDirSt</SHORT-NAME>
				  <LONG-NAME>
					<L-4 L="EN">Engine: Engine Running Direction State</L-4>
				  </LONG-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">EngRunngDir1</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>EngStrtRemReq1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Remote Engine Start Request 1</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Information to start the engine from a remote control</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>EngStrtReq</SHORT-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">EngStrtRemReq1</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>EngT1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Engine: Engine Temperature</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Consolidated engine temperature.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">For engines with water cooling systems, the signal shows the coolant temperature.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Example for the accuracy requirement on this signal in a typical series project: ±5 K.
The accuracy requirement is a „goal“.
Project-specific requirements must be defined in close cooperation with transmission and engine engineering.</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>EngT</SHORT-NAME>
				  <LONG-NAME>
					<L-4 L="EN">Engine: Engine Temperature</L-4>
				  </LONG-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">T4</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqCluMin1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Minimum Engine Torque at Clutch</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Minimum engine torque at clutch level of not fired engine at current engine speed.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Minimum engine torque at clutch considers following contributors if present
1) internal engine torque losses like friction, pumping, mechanical driven water pump etc.
2) losses with influence on torque at clutch caused by alternator, airconditioning, power steering etc.
Loss differences from engine to engine and variable torque losses over life cycle have to be considered.
Usually this signal corresponds to the drag torque of the combustion engine at current speed.</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqCluMin</SHORT-NAME>
				  <LONG-NAME>
					<L-4 L="EN">Minimum Engine Torque at Clutch</L-4>
				  </LONG-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME NAME-PATTERN="{anyName}">EngTqCluStrtPred1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Engine: Predicted Clutch Torque to Start the Engine</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Predicted torque necessary to start the combustion engine by slipstart.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">This signal must be provided from engine start until a project-dependent combustion engine speed.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">The calculation of this signal must consider the influences on this start torque, for example:</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Additionally, from standstill until the first expansion stroke, the signal must include the predicted maximum torque that is necessary to overcome the first compression stroke.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">The calculation of this signal by the provider is not permitted to consider the inertia, which has an effect on the torque at clutch. This means that the signal must be calculated as if the inertia is 0 kg*(m^2).</L-1>
				</P>
				<LIST TYPE="UNNUMBER">
				  <ITEM>
					<P>
					  <L-1 L="EN">sticking friction and sliding friction,</L-1>
					</P>
				  </ITEM>
				  <ITEM>
					<P>
					  <L-1 L="EN">compression effects depending on crankshaft angle,</L-1>
					</P>
				  </ITEM>
				  <ITEM>
					<P>
					  <L-1 L="EN">auxiliaries and ancillaries/PTO,</L-1>
					</P>
				  </ITEM>
				  <ITEM>
					<P>
					  <L-1 L="EN">combustion engine temperature,</L-1>
					</P>
				  </ITEM>
				  <ITEM>
					<P>
					  <L-1 L="EN">coolant temperature.</L-1>
					</P>
				  </ITEM>
				</LIST>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqCluStrtPred</SHORT-NAME>
				  <LONG-NAME>
					<L-4 L="EN">Engine: Predicted Clutch Torque to Start the Engine</L-4>
				  </LONG-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqCrksft1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Engine: Torque at Crankshaft</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Indicated torque of combustion engine plus internal engine torque losses. The effect of inertia on the torque is not considered.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Torque at crankshaft considers the following contributors, if present:
1) Indicated torque of combustion engine, calculated based on injection timing and injected fuel, ignition angle and air mass.
2) Internal engine torque losses such as friction, pumping, mechanically driven water pump, etc.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Ancillary torque losses caused by the alternator, air conditioning, power steering, etc., are not considered.
The calculation of this signal by the provider is not permitted to consider the inertia, which has an effect on the torque at clutch. This means that the signal must be calculated as if the inertia is 0 kg*(m^2).
Loss differences from engine to engine and variable torque losses over the life cycle must be considered.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">The signal includes all torque requests from the accelerator pedal, cruise control, speed limiter, etc., and all interventions, e.g., torque and speed interventions.
Example of implementation:
The torque is a cylinder average, not a time average, via two crankshaft revolutions of all cylinders, in consideration of the current operating parameters. The operating parameters include the engine temperature, ignition timing and air mass measured or calculated, lambda, fuel cut level, fuel quantity, injection timing, knock control adaption, geographic altitude and others.</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqCrksft</SHORT-NAME>
				  <LONG-NAME>
					<L-4 L="EN">Engine: Torque at Crankshaft</L-4>
				  </LONG-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqCrksftMax1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Maximum Available Engine Torque at Crankshaft</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">The maximum torque at crankshaft at the current engine speed and actual air mass (both gasoline and diesel), including the static power limitation of the engine (e.g. calibrated restrictions for engine protection)</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Example of realization: The maximum torque is realized by fast and slow path [e.g. with the earliest possible ignition angle at current lambda (gasoline in homogeneous mode) or the maximum fuel mass and injection timing (diesel)] including average knocking (average of cylinders), smoke limitation.''''''</L-1>
				</P>
				<LIST TYPE="UNNUMBER">
				  <ITEM>
					<P>
					  <L-1 L="EN">The signal is valid if the engine speed is higher than a certain engine speed threshold. This threshold depends on the engine (e.g. about 500 rpm for four cylinder engines). Below this limit the accuracy of this value may decrease significantly. </L-1>
					</P>
				  </ITEM>
				  <ITEM>
					<P>
					  <L-1 L="EN">For hybrid stop/start strategy the engine speed of the fired engine should always be above the speed threshold. </L-1>
					</P>
				  </ITEM>
				  <ITEM>
					<P>
					  <L-1 L="EN">Default value after reset is zero</L-1>
					</P>
				  </ITEM>
				</LIST>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqCrksftMax</SHORT-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqCrksftMaxEngNCur1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Engine: Maximum Torque at Crankshaft at Current Engine Speed</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Maximum possible torque at crankshaft at current speed with maximum possible air mass at current ambient pressure and air temperature, including static power limitation of the engine.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Theoretical full load engine torque at crankshaft at current engine speed. Maximally charged for turbo systems.
The static power limitation contains, e.g., restrictions for protection and static soot limitation.
Permanent knock limitation is considered, knock control is not considered.</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqCrksftMaxEngNCur</SHORT-NAME>
				  <LONG-NAME>
					<L-4 L="EN">Engine: Maximum Torque at Crankshaft at Current Engine Speed</L-4>
				  </LONG-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqCrksftMaxFast1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Maximum Engine Torque at Crankshaft Fast Path</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Maximum engine torque at crankshaft fast path including current engine speed, the actual air mass (both gasoline and diesel) and the static power limitation of the engine (e.g. calibrated restrictions for engine protection). This signal is relevant for torque requests realized by fast path.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Example of realization: The maximum torque is realized by fast path [e.g. with the earliest possible ignition angle at current lambda (gasoline in homogeneous mode) or the maximum fuel mass and optimum injection timing concerning torque (diesel)], including average knocking (average of cylinders), smoke limitation.</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqCrksftMaxFast</SHORT-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqCrksftMaxOptmCdn1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Maximum Engine Torque at Crankshaft at Optimum Conditions</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">The maximum torque at crankshaft at the current engine speed, maximum air mass, current ambient pressure and air temperature (both gasoline and diesel), including the static power limitation of the engine (e.g. calibrated restrictions for engine protection). It is calculated for ideal conditions.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Example of Realization: The maximum torque is realized by fast and slow path [e.g. with the earliest possible ignition angle at optimum lambda concerning torque (gasoline) or the maximum fuel mass and injection timing (diesel)]. Smoke limitation is included in the signal. Average knocking is not considered (without knock control), but the precalibrated knocking limitation.''''''</L-1>
				</P>
				<LIST TYPE="UNNUMBER">
				  <ITEM>
					<P>
					  <L-1 L="EN">The signal is valid if the engine speed is higher than a certain engine speed threshold. This threshold depends on the engine (e.g. about 500 rpm for four cylinder engines). Below this limit the accuracy of this value may decrease significantly. </L-1>
					</P>
				  </ITEM>
				  <ITEM>
					<P>
					  <L-1 L="EN">For hybrid stop/start strategy the engine speed of the fired engine should always be above the speed threshold. </L-1>
					</P>
				  </ITEM>
				  <ITEM>
					<P>
					  <L-1 L="EN">Default value after reset is zero</L-1>
					</P>
				  </ITEM>
				</LIST>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqCrksftMaxOptmCdn</SHORT-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqCrksftMaxProtn1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Maximum Allowed Torque at Crankshaft for Engine Protection</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Maximum crankshaft torque including engine protection. If no protection function is active, the value of this interface will be the upper limit of the chosen data type.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Example of realization: Including catalyst protection, over heating, intake air system protection and fail safe etc.signal is sent with initialisation</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqCrksftMaxProtn</SHORT-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqCrksftMaxSpdCur1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Engine: Maximum Torque at Crankshaft at Current Speed</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Maximum possible torque at crankshaft at current speed with maximum possible air mass at current ambient pressure and air temperature, including static power limitation of the engine.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Theoretical full load engine torque at crankshaft at actual engine speed. Maximally charged for turbo systems.
Static power limitation contains e.g. restrictions for protection and static smoke limitation.
Permanent knock limitation is considered, knock control not.</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqCrksftMaxSpdCur</SHORT-NAME>
				  <LONG-NAME>
					<L-4 L="EN">Engine: Maximum Torque at Crankshaft at Current Speed</L-4>
				  </LONG-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqCrksftMin1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Engine: Minimum Engine Torque at Crankshaft Considering Engine Internal Torque Losses</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Minimum engine torque at crankshaft level of not fired engine at current engine speed.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">The minimum engine torque at crankshaft considers the internal engine torque losses such as friction, pumping, mechanically driven water pump, etc.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Loss differences from engine to engine and variable torque losses over the life cycle must be considered.
Usually, this signal corresponds to the drag torque of the combustion engine at current speed.</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqCrksftMin</SHORT-NAME>
				  <LONG-NAME>
					<L-4 L="EN">Engine: Minimum Engine Torque at Crankshaft Considering Engine Internal Torque Losses</L-4>
				  </LONG-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqCrksftMinBasc1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Minimum Engine Torque at Crankshaft for Powertrain Realized by Slow Path</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">The minimum torque at crankshaft at the current engine speed and the minimum air mass (both gasoline and diesel) not including spark retard (gasoline) and fuel cut off.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Example of realization: The minimum torque is realized by slow path [e.g. normal ignition timing for the minimum mass air at current lambda (gasoline homogeneous) or the minimum fuel mass and injection timing (diesel)]. For diesel engines this interface is possibly equivalent to the torque losses, because minimum fuel mass could be zero. Otherwise minimum torque for fired engine.''''''</L-1>
				</P>
				<LIST TYPE="UNNUMBER">
				  <ITEM>
					<P>
					  <L-1 L="EN">The signal is valid if the engine speed is higher than a certain engine speed threshold. This threshold depends on the engine (e.g. about 500 rpm for four cylinder engines). Below this limit the accuracy of this value may decrease significantly. </L-1>
					</P>
				  </ITEM>
				  <ITEM>
					<P>
					  <L-1 L="EN">For hybrid stop/start strategy the engine speed of the fired engine should always be above the speed threshold. </L-1>
					</P>
				  </ITEM>
				  <ITEM>
					<P>
					  <L-1 L="EN">Default value after reset is zero</L-1>
					</P>
				  </ITEM>
				</LIST>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqCrksftMinBasc</SHORT-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqCrksftMinFast1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Engine: Minimum Torque at Crankshaft Fast Path</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Minimum torque at crankshaft of combustion engine at latest possible ignition angle. Calculated at current engine speed with current air mass, current ambient pressure and current air temperature.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Signal is relevant for gasoline engines only.
The latest possible ignition angle, also called "max. ignition retard", depends on exhaust temperature, catalyst protection, etc.
A torque decrease request from the transmission down to this torque level should only be implemented by ignition retard and not by cylinder cut off.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">For diesel engines, this signal depends on the minimum fuel mass, which is usually zero.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">In parallel hybrid projects, this is the minimum torque the combustion engine can implement.</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqCrksftMinFast</SHORT-NAME>
				  <LONG-NAME>
					<L-4 L="EN">Engine: Minimum Torque at Crankshaft Fast Path</L-4>
				  </LONG-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqCrksftMinWoCutOff1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Minimum Engine Torque at Crankshaft for Powertrain Realized by Slow and Fast Path</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">The minimum torque at crankshaft at the current engine speed and the minimum air mass (both gasoline and diesel) including spark retard (gasoline), not including fuel cut off.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Example of realization: The minimum torque is realized by slow and fast path [e.g. considering a certain spark retard for the minimum air mass at current lambda (gasoline homogeneous) or the minimum fuel mass and injection timing (diesel)]. The possible amount of spark retard can be defined depending on the application, e.g. according to drive ability criteria. For diesel engines this interface is possibly equivalent to the torque losses, because minimum fuel mass could be zero. Otherwise minimum torque for fired engine.''''''</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">cylinder engines). Below this limit the accuracy of this value may decrease significantly. </L-1>
				</P>
				<LIST TYPE="UNNUMBER">
				  <ITEM>
					<P>
					  <L-1 L="EN">The signal is valid if the engine speed is higher than a certain engine speed threshold. This threshold depends on the engine (e.g. about 500 rpm for four </L-1>
					</P>
				  </ITEM>
				</LIST>
				<LIST TYPE="UNNUMBER">
				  <ITEM>
					<P>
					  <L-1 L="EN">For hybrid stop/start strategy the engine speed of the fired engine should always be above the speed threshold. </L-1>
					</P>
				  </ITEM>
				  <ITEM>
					<P>
					  <L-1 L="EN">Default value after reset is zero</L-1>
					</P>
				  </ITEM>
				</LIST>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqCrksftMinWoCutOff</SHORT-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqCrksftRedByAncllryLoss1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Engine: Torque at Crankshaft Reduced by Ancillary Losses</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Torque at crankshaft reduced by ancillary losses.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Indicated engine torque calculated based on injection timing and injected fuel, ignition angle and air mass, plus
1) Internal engine torque losses such as friction, pumping, mechanically driven water pump, etc.
2) Ancillary torque losses with an effect on torque at crankshaft caused by i.a., alternator, air conditioning, power steering.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">The calculation of this signal by the provider is not permitted to consider the inertia, which has an effect on the torque at clutch. This means that the signal must be calculated as if the inertia is 0 kg*(m^2).</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">In series, loss differences from engine to engine and variable torque losses over the life cycle must be considered.</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqCrksftRedByAncllryLoss</SHORT-NAME>
				  <LONG-NAME>
					<L-4 L="EN">Engine: Torque at Crankshaft Reduced by Ancillary Losses</L-4>
				  </LONG-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqCrksftRedByAncllryLossMin1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Engine: Minimum Torque at Crankshaft Reduced by Ancillary Losses</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Minimum engine torque at crankshaft of not fired engine at current engine speed decreased by ancillary losses.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">The minimum engine torque at crankshaft considers the following contributors, if present:
1) Internal engine torque losses such as friction, pumping, mechanically driven water pump, etc.
2) Ancillary torque losses with an effect on torque at crankshaft caused by i.a., alternator, air conditioning, power steering.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">In series, loss differences from engine to engine and variable torque losses over the life cycle must be considered.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Usually, this signal corresponds to the drag torque of the combustion engine at current speed.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Example for timing and accuracy requirements in a typical series project: Max. 40 ms delay time, accuracy: ±7 % or ±5 Nm (max. selection), max. deviation ±20 Nm.</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqCrksftRedByAncllryLossMin</SHORT-NAME>
				  <LONG-NAME>
					<L-4 L="EN">Engine: Minimum Torque at Crankshaft Reduced by Ancillary Losses</L-4>
				  </LONG-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqDecAtCluReqByEscFast1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Engine Torque Decrease at Clutch Request by ESC Fast</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Decreased engine torque at clutch requested by Electronic stability control below the driver input torque including virtual driver request. Fast refers to the immediate / instant torque request, typically achieved by ignition timing.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqDecAtCluReqByEscFast</SHORT-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqDecAtCluReqByEscSlow1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Engine Torque Decrease at Clutch Request by ESC Slow</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Decreased engine torque at clutch requested by Electronic stability control below the driver input torque including virtual driver request. Slow refers to the longer term or torque reserve request, usually the input to throttle control.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqDecAtCluReqByEscSlow</SHORT-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqIncAtCluReqByEsc1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Engine Torque Increase at Clutch Request by ESC</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Increased engine torque at clutch requested by Electronic stability control over the driver input torque including virtual driver request.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqIncAtCluReqByEsc</SHORT-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqJCrksft1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Engine: Engine Torque of Inertia at Crankshaft</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Inertia torque of combustion engine at clutch level. Definition of the sign: An increasing speed produces a negative sign; a decreasing speed produces a positive sign.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">The signal contains the dynamic torque caused by the inertia, which increases or decreases the torque at clutch.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">The engine internal inertia and the inertia of the ancillaries up to the clutch must be considered.</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqJCrksft</SHORT-NAME>
				  <LONG-NAME>
					<L-4 L="EN">Engine: Engine Torque of Inertia at Crankshaft</L-4>
				  </LONG-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqResvPt1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Torque Reserve Request from Engine to Powertrain</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Reserved torque request to be coordinated by the Powertrain Coordinator (PTC). This reserved torque could be realized either by the combustion engine or by another torque source (e.g. electric motor in a hybrid system). It does not include reserved torque requests which will be coordinated inside the combustion engine, e.g. torque reserve for catalyst heating or torque reserve to realize a change in the engine operation mode.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Default value after reset is zero</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqResvPt</SHORT-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqResvReqPt1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Torque Reserve Request from Engine to Powertrain</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Reserved torque request to be coordinated by the Powertrain Coordinator (PTC). This reserved torque could be realized either by the combustion engine or by another torque source (e.g. electric motor in a hybrid system). It does not include reserved torque requests which will be coordinated inside the combustion engine, e.g. torque reserve for catalyst heating or torque reserve to realize a change in the engine operation mode.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Default value after reset is zero.</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>EngTqResvReqPt</SHORT-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
