			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>InclnSts1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Inclination Status</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Information given to know the inclination of the vehicle in order to adapt the beam of the exterior lights</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>Sts</SHORT-NAME>
				  <DESC>
					<L-2 L="EN">value greater than 100% means invalid; initial value = value greater than 100%</L-2>
				  </DESC>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Perc2</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>IndcrDisp1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Indicator Display</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Turn indicator activation status on cluster</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>St</SHORT-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">IndcrSt1</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>IndcrTurnCmd1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Indicator Turn Command</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Command to turn on or off the turn indicators according to a requested pattern.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>Cmd</SHORT-NAME>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>IndcrTurnReq1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Indicator Turn Request</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Demand to activate / deactivate left or right indicator blinking or temporary blinking left / right. As long as direction indication is requested, the corresponding value should be set. The temporary information can be generated by the sensor component due to special switches or by an adapter component generating it due to timing calculations.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>Req</SHORT-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">IndcrTypExt1</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>IntrLiReq1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Interior Light Request</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Request to activate / deactivate an interior light actuator or a virtual interior light group. Faulty switch requires (in-band) invalidation. Also there might be a separate value required for initialization.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">This interface is not necessary for each interior light actuator; it is not intended for hardwired interior lights.</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>Req</SHORT-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">IntrLiReq1</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>KeyInsertSt1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Key Insert Status</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">state whether the key is inserted into key cylinder or not</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>KeyInsertSt</SHORT-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">KeyInsertSt1</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>KeyInsertSts1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Key Insert Status</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">state whether the key is inserted into key cylinder or not</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>KeyInsertSts</SHORT-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">KeyInsertSts1</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>KnobRotyBndlsStep15</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Boundless Rotary Knob 15 Steps</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">user input to system: The value represents the relative number of steps/positions (out of 15 values) the knob has been moved since the last reported movement. Positive values denote clockwise, negative counter clockwise rotation.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>Step</SHORT-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Nr1</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>KnobRotyBndlsStep7</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Boundless Rotary Knob 7 Steps</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">user input to system: The value represents the relative number of steps/positions (out of 7 values) the knob has been moved since the last reported movement. Positive values denote clockwise, negative counter clockwise rotation.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>Step</SHORT-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Nr9</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>LedCmd1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Led Command</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Command to activate the Antitheft Warning System (ATWS) Light Emitting Diode (LED) on board</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>Cmd</SHORT-NAME>
				  <DESC>
					<L-2 L="EN">OFF - LED not requested by alarm ON - LED requested by alarm</L-2>
				  </DESC>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">OnOff1</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>LiDimGlbCmd1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Light Dim Global Command</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">This is the command of light master to give a global exterior and interior light dimming information based on the outside brightness level. It is used e. g. to dim the exterior light depending on outside brightness.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">0% means full darkness
100% means maximum brightness
This interface gives the information of the actual outside brightness. E.g. exterior or interior light can use this information to adapt their own dimming calculation.</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>Cmd</SHORT-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Perc2</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>LiExtCmd1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Exterior Light Command</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Generic command from light manager to light adapter components to turn on/off selected lights.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>Cmd</SHORT-NAME>
				  <DESC>
					<L-2 L="EN">Turning On or OFF</L-2>
				  </DESC>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">OnOff1</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>LiExtReq1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Light External Request</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Generic exterior lights request</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>Req</SHORT-NAME>
				  <DESC>
					<L-2 L="EN">Turning On or OFF</L-2>
				  </DESC>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">OnOff1</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>LiFltSt1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Light Fault Status</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Used as feedback from an actuator component to indicate that the light source is broken or not.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Note that no details of the fault are transmitted, but just an operational / defective fault indication. This enables a control component to decide whether a broken light has to be replaced by another light source.The interface is not used for detailed diagnostics.
If the light source contains more than one e. g. bulb, it shall be defined how many actuators have to be broken to reach the state defective. The decision to give the status defective is done by the actuator component</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>St</SHORT-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">DevErrSt2</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>LiFltSts1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Light Fault Status</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Used as feedback from an actuator component to indicate that the light source is broken or not.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Note that no details of the fault are transmitted, but just an operational / defective fault indication. This enables a control component to decide whether a broken light has to be replaced by another light source.The interface is not used for detailed diagnostics.
If the light source contains more than one e. g. bulb, it shall be defined how many actuators have to be broken to reach the state defective. The decision to give the status defective is done by the actuator component</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>Sts</SHORT-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">DevErrSts2</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
