				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>Sts</SHORT-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">OpendClsd1</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>OperModSt1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Operation Mode Status</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">This interface provides the vehicle operation states. It can be seen as an abstraction and extension of the normal ignition switch position (also called "clamp position") which is traditionally used to guide functional operation of the vehicle. It also includes information about what state the engine is in, i.e. running or not. This interface should be used to control which functionalities / components are active in the vehicle. All states have to be implemented in all vehicles, but not necessarily used.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>St</SHORT-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">OperModSt1</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>OperModSts1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Operation Mode Status</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">This interface provides the vehicle operation states. It can be seen as an abstraction and extension of the normal ignition switch position (also called "clamp position") which is traditionally used to guide functional operation of the vehicle. It also includes information about what state the engine is in, i.e. running or not. This interface should be used to control which functionalities / components are active in the vehicle. All states have to be implemented in all vehicles, but not necessarily used.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>Sts</SHORT-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">OperModSts1</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>OutdBriSt1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Outside Brightness Status</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">This is the outside brightness quantized in some levels. It is e.g. used by exterior light master to provide a global exterior and interior dimming information based on the outside brightness</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
