				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>PtAccrPedlPosn1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Powertrain: Accelerator Pedal Position</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Accelerator pedal position. Accelerator pedal ratio shaped and filtered.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">The calibration must ensure that the used signal range is 0 – 100 %.
0 % is driver off the pedal, offsets are removed. 100 % must be ensured at end point of the pedal.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Consolidated physical value, either a measured value (Measd) or a modeled value (Estimd). Final filtered and offset-corrected consolidated actuator value/physical sensor value. Virtual physical sensor value/fused sensor value that comes as close as possible to the technical signal. If it is not possible to provide a physical sensor value (e.g. failure, implausibility or other reasons), then a substitute value/default value or a frozen value is provided.</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>PtAccrPedlPosn</SHORT-NAME>
				  <LONG-NAME>
					<L-4 L="EN">Powertrain: Accelerator Pedal Position</L-4>
				  </LONG-NAME>
				  <DESC/>
				  <INTRODUCTION/>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Perc1</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>PtAccrPedlPosnVirt1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Powertrain: Virtual Accelerator Pedal Position</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Theoretical accelerator pedal value determined using the physical pedal value and requests from Adaptive Cruise Control or Cruise Control etc.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Example of implementation: Within Adaptive Cruise Control / Cruise Control, this is based on the total requested propulsion wheel torque from the driver or the Vehicle Longitudinal Control, otherwise, this is the "Accelerator Pedal Ratio" value.
Evaluated signal, jitter free, including plausibility check, monitoring and substitute value but without filtering.
0 %: (Virtual) driver is off the pedal, offsets are removed. 100 %: Must be ensured at end point of the pedal. Must cover the 100 % as well.</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>PtAccrPedlPosnVirt</SHORT-NAME>
				  <LONG-NAME>
					<L-4 L="EN">Powertrain: Virtual Accelerator Pedal Position</L-4>
				  </LONG-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Perc1</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>PtCluEngTqMaxCluPCur1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Powertrain: Engine Clutch Maximum Torque at Current Clutch Pressure</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Maximum transmittable torque of engine clutch at current pressure.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">No further explanation needed.</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>PtCluEngTqMaxCluPCur</SHORT-NAME>
				  <LONG-NAME>
					<L-4 L="EN">Powertrain: Engine Clutch Maximum Torque at Current Clutch Pressure</L-4>
				  </LONG-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME NAME-PATTERN="{anyName}">PtDrvrReqTqClu1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Powertrain: Driver Request of Torque at Clutch</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Torque at clutch requested by the driver.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Combination of all real and virtual driver requests, project specific including idle speed control. Virtual driver requests include cruise control, distance cruise control, vehicle speed limiter, etc.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">This signal shows the unfiltered driver requested torque and therefore it is not affected by driving comfort functions. The signal determines the earliest torque information in the torque chain architecture.
Used to prepare transmission internal system functions to achieve a proper spontaneity according to the driver request.
Predicted torque information, which is determined based on the driver pedal position or on driver assistance systems.
Independent of whether the engine is running or not, this signal always delivers the torque information as if the engine is running.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">The calculation of this signal by the provider is not permitted to consider the inertia, which has an effect on the torque at clutch. This means that the signal must be calculated as if the inertia is 0 kg*(m^2).</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">In hybrid projects, a limitation by the torque of the engine clutch is not visible.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">In projects with engine clutch, this signal is not permitted to be limited due to the state of the engine clutch.</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>PtDrvrReqTqClu</SHORT-NAME>
				  <LONG-NAME>
					<L-4 L="EN">Powertrain: Driver Request of Torque at Clutch</L-4>
				  </LONG-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME NAME-PATTERN="{anyName}">PtDrvrReqTqCluPredEngN1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Powertrain: Predicted Driver Request of Torque at Clutch in Target Speed</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Predicted driver requested torque at clutch at the engine speed reached in target gear.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Environmental conditions, such as altitude and temperature and engine internal limits, e.g., smoke limitation and full load limit, are considered.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">The calculation of this signal by the provider is not permitted to consider the inertia, which has an effect on the torque at clutch. This means that the signal must be calculated as if the inertia is 0 kg*(m^2).</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">The calculation of this signal is based on signal See also: “Transmission: Predicted Virtual Clutch Speed in Target Gear”.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">References to other signals:
TrsmCluNPredGearTarTrsmCluNVirtGearTar</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>PtDrvrReqTqCluPredEngN</SHORT-NAME>
				  <LONG-NAME>
					<L-4 L="EN">Powertrain: Predicted Driver Request of Torque at Clutch in Target Speed</L-4>
				  </LONG-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>PtEmTq1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Powertrain: Electric Machine Torque</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Torque of the electric machine at clutch.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Torque output of the electric machine at clutch level. The gear ratio between the electric machine shaft and the clutch, if present, must be considered.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">The calculation of this signal by the provider is not permitted to consider the inertia, which has an effect on the torque at clutch. This means that the signal must be calculated as if the inertia is 0 kg*(m^2).</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Timing and accuracy requirements on this torque signal have to be defined in close cooperation of engine and transmission experts, especially for combined engine and electric machine operation.</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>PtEmTq</SHORT-NAME>
				  <LONG-NAME>
					<L-4 L="EN">Powertrain: Electric Machine Torque</L-4>
				  </LONG-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>PtEmTqJRotorShaft1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Powertrain: Electric Machine Torque of Inertia at Rotor Shaft</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Inertia torque of the electric machine at clutch level. Definition of the sign: An increasing speed produces a negative sign; a decreasing speed produces a positive sign.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">The signal contains the dynamic torque caused by the inertia of the electric machine, which, in parallel hybrid projects, increases or decreases the torque at clutch.</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>PtEmTqJRotorShaft</SHORT-NAME>
				  <LONG-NAME>
					<L-4 L="EN">Powertrain: Electric Machine Torque of Inertia at Rotor Shaft</L-4>
				  </LONG-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>PtEmTqMaxCluNCur1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Powertrain: Electric Machine Maximum Torque at Current Clutch Speed</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Maximum possible torque of electric machine at clutch at current clutch speed and current operating point, including all system limitations.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Theoretical maximum possible torque output of the electric machine at clutch level with maximum possible inverter phase electric current. The current operating point is defined e.g., by the current DC-link voltage, the rotor temperature and the battery power. System limitations are, e.g., speed limits, temperature limits, electric current limits and voltage limits. The gear ratio between the electric machine shaft and the clutch is considered.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">The calculation of this signal by the provider is not permitted to consider the inertia, which has an effect on the torque at clutch. This means that the signal must be calculated as if the inertia is 0 kg*(m^2).</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>PtEmTqMaxCluNCur</SHORT-NAME>
				  <LONG-NAME>
					<L-4 L="EN">Powertrain: Electric Machine Maximum Torque at Current Clutch Speed</L-4>
				  </LONG-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>PtEmTqMinCluNCur1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Powertrain: Electric Machine Minimum Torque at Current Clutch Speed</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Minimum possible torque of electric machine at clutch at current clutch speed and current operating point, including all system limitations.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Theoretical minimum possible torque output of the electric machine at clutch level with maximum possible inverter phase electric current. The current operating point is defined e.g., by the current DC-link voltage, the rotor temperature and the battery power. System limitations are, e.g., speed limits, temperature limits, electric current limits and voltage limits. The gear ratio between the electric machine shaft and the clutch is considered.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">The calculation of this signal by the provider is not permitted to consider the inertia, which has an effect on the torque at clutch. This means that the signal must be calculated as if the inertia is 0 kg*(m^2).</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>PtEmTqMinCluNCur</SHORT-NAME>
				  <LONG-NAME>
					<L-4 L="EN">Powertrain: Electric Machine Minimum Torque at Current Clutch Speed</L-4>
				  </LONG-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME NAME-PATTERN="{anyName}">PtEmTqRelCluReq1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Powertrain: Electric Machine Relative Torque at Clutch Requested by Powertrain</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Electric machine relative torque at clutch requested by powertrain.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Torque to be implemented by the electric machine additional to the driver requested torque.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Typically used to create the electric machine torque which is necessary to start the combustion engine via the engine clutch without influencing the implementation of the driver requested torque.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">As long as there is no torque request, the signal "Powertrain: Implementation Type of Electric Machine Relative Torque at Clutch Requested by Powertrain” is “0h = no request” and signal "Powertrain: Electric Machine Relative Torque at Clutch Requested by Powertrain” is “FFEh = Init”.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">This signal is closely related to signal “Powertrain: Implementation Type of the Electric Machine Relative Torque at Clutch Requested by Powertrain”.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">References to other signals:
PtNrTypEmTqRelCluReq</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>PtEmTqRelCluReq</SHORT-NAME>
				  <LONG-NAME>
					<L-4 L="EN">Powertrain: Electric Machine Relative Torque at Clutch Requested by Powertrain</L-4>
				  </LONG-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>PtEmTqReq1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Powertrain: Requested Electric Machine Torque</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Requested electric machine torque, including all interventions, including all limitations.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">The signal contains the limitations which are closely related to the electric machine or which are attributed to the electric machine by the powertrain coordinator.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">The content of this signal is related to the clutch level, so a possibly installed ratio between the rotor of the electric machine and the clutch is considered.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">The calculation of this signal by the provider is not permitted to consider the inertia, which has an effect on the torque at clutch. This means that the signal must be calculated as if the inertia is 0 kg*(m^2).</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">The signal contains all interventions.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">The goal is that the torque information is sent 50 – 80 ms ahead of the desired real/physical torque.</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>PtEmTqReq</SHORT-NAME>
				  <LONG-NAME>
					<L-4 L="EN">Powertrain: Requested Electric Machine Torque</L-4>
				  </LONG-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>PtEmTqResvReq1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Powertrain: Torque Reserve Electric Machine Requested by Powertrain</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Torque reserve of the electric machine, might be used to start the combustion engine.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">This torque reserve is the sum of “Engine: Minimum Torque at Crankshaft Reduced by Ancillary Losses” and the torque necessary to compensate for the inertia, if it is used to start the combustion engine.
If no torque reserve is necessary, then the signal is set to 0 Nm.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">References to other signals:
EngTqCrksftRedByAncllryLossMin</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>PtEmTqResvReq</SHORT-NAME>
				  <LONG-NAME>
					<L-4 L="EN">Powertrain: Torque Reserve Electric Machine Requested by Powertrain</L-4>
				  </LONG-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>PtFlgAcDeactvt1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Powertrain: Request to Deactivate Air Conditioner (A/C)</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Request to deactivate Air Conditioner (A/C) 0 = no deactivation of A/C requested 1 = deactivation of A/C requested</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>PtFlgAcDeactvtReq1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Powertrain: Request to Deactivate Air Conditioner (A/C)</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Request to deactivate Air Conditioner (A/C) 0 = no deactivation of A/C requested 1 = deactivation of A/C requested.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>PtFlgAcDeactvtReq</SHORT-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Flg1</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
