			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME NAME-PATTERN="{anyName}">TrsmTiCluNReqTar1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Transmission: Target Time to Reach Clutch Speed Requested by Transmission</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Target time to reach clutch speed requested by transmission.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">The speed at clutch requested by "Transmission: Clutch Speed Requested by Transmission" must be reached in the transmitted target time.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">As long as there is no speed request, the recommendation is to send the initialization value.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">References to other signals:
TrsmCluNReq</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>TrsmTiCluNReqTar</SHORT-NAME>
				  <LONG-NAME>
					<L-4 L="EN">Transmission: Target Time to Reach Clutch Speed Requested by Transmission</L-4>
				  </LONG-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Ti3</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME NAME-PATTERN="{anyName}">TrsmTqCluGbxCnsNIdleCtrlr1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Transmission: Gearbox Torque Consumption at Clutch for Idle Speed Controller</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Gearbox torque at clutch consumption based on transmission oil pump torque losses and drive-off element torque.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">The torque consumed by the gearbox must be provided to the engine to ensure stable idle speed operation.
Together with other torque losses, it significantly contributes to the idle speed controller setpoint, especially if there is no driver torque request.
Consequently it is used for precontrol in the idle speed controller and defines an essential part of the minimum limit for the driver torque request.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">The gearbox torque consumption is
a) the sum of the drive-off element torque and the absolute value of the transmission oil pump torque losses, if the propulsion unit is in idle speed, the vehicle is at a standstill and there is no driver torque request.
Especially the drive-off element torque depends on the targeted state of power transmission of the gearbox, which is determined primarily by the gear lever position.
b) the absolute value of the transmission oil pump torque losses, if the drive-off element is closed.
c) a combination of a) and b) depending on the propulsion unit speed, vehicle speed and gearbox control strategy in all other situations.
In this case, this signal might even be greater than the torque value of a) because the propulsion unit speed is greater than the idle speed. But the combination is limited by a powertrain torque limit. If the torque at clutch is greater than this limit, then this signal is less than the real/physical torque at clutch.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">A typical behavior is that the summated torque a) at vehicle standstill is ramped to the transmission oil pump torque b). The ramp depends on the vehicle speed and reaches b) at low vehicle speeds, e.g., 7km/h. The transition from idle speed to driving usually is completed at this velocity.</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>TrsmTqCluGbxCnsNIdleCtrlr</SHORT-NAME>
				  <LONG-NAME>
					<L-4 L="EN">Transmission: Gearbox Torque Consumption at Clutch for Idle Speed Controller</L-4>
				  </LONG-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>TrsmTqCluGrdtUpprLimReq1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Transmission: Clutch Torque Gradient Upper Limit Requested by Transmission</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Transmission request to limit the clutch torque gradient if changes in the real and virtual driver requests could cause the clutch torque gradient to be greater than the specified limit.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Transmission request to limit the clutch torque gradient if changes in the real and virtual driver requests could cause the clutch torque gradient to be greater than the specified limit. Other requests such as engine internal stall protection and idle speed control or other external interventions, are not permitted to be limited.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">This signal offers the following benefit in comparison to the transmission torque requests:</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">The effect of the signal must be visible on signals
"Powertrain: Torque at Clutch",
"Powertrain: Torque at Clutch without Transmission Intervention",
"Powertrain: Requested Torque at Clutch without Transmission Intervention",
“Powertrain: Predicted Driver Request of Torque at Clutch in Target Speed”.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">As a default value, or if there is no request from the transmission, the passive value (FEh) is sent.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">The target is to implement this gradient limitation as fast as possible by fast and slow request.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">For “Mild Hybrids” and “Full Hybrids” (Parallel Hybrids), the transmission transmits the “gradient of the summarized torque request of combustion engine and electric machine”. For “Full Hybrids” (Parallel Hybrids), the torque transmitted by the engine clutch must be considered.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">References to other signals:
PtTqClu
PtTqCluWoTrsmIntv
PtTqCluReqWoTrsmIntv
PtDrvrReqTqCluPredEngN</L-1>
				</P>
				<LIST TYPE="UNNUMBER">
				  <ITEM>
					<P>
					  <L-1 L="EN">homogenous transition without torque jumps,</L-1>
					</P>
				  </ITEM>
				  <ITEM>
					<P>
					  <L-1 L="EN">preventive protection without unintended effects on driving behavior,</L-1>
					</P>
				  </ITEM>
				  <ITEM>
					<P>
					  <L-1 L="EN">improvement of dynamics in comparison to limitation by the transmission torque requests.</L-1>
					</P>
				  </ITEM>
				</LIST>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>TrsmTqCluGrdtUpprLimReq</SHORT-NAME>
				  <LONG-NAME>
					<L-4 L="EN">Transmission: Clutch Torque Gradient Upper Limit Requested by Transmission</L-4>
				  </LONG-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">TqGrdt1</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>TrsmTqCluLoss1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Transmission: Transmission Torque Losses at Clutch</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Transmission torque losses at clutch.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">The transmission torque losses include the torque of the gearbox oil pump and gearbox internal losses, e.g., bearing friction and drag torque losses of clutches.
Torque losses occurring at a shaft with a speed different from the clutch speed must be converted to clutch speed considering the relevant transmission ratio.
Typically, the values are from test bench measurements.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">These losses are usually considered when converting engine to wheel torque and vice versa.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">In projects in which the differential and transfer case and/or reduction gearbox are integrated in the transmission housing, the signal also considers the losses of these components.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">The value sent on the network is the absolute value of the transmission torque losses.
The value on the application level must consider the sign. The Application Data Type must cover negative values.</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>TrsmTqCluLoss</SHORT-NAME>
				  <LONG-NAME>
					<L-4 L="EN">Transmission: Transmission Torque Losses at Clutch</L-4>
				  </LONG-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq6</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME NAME-PATTERN="{anyName}">TrsmTqCluMaxFastReqForShiftIntv1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Transmission: Request for Maximum Torque at Clutch for Shift Intervention on Fast Path</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Maximum torque at clutch requested by transmission for shift intervention on fast path.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Usually used for shift intervention, but permitted for all purposes.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">As long as there is no torque request from the transmission, a constant substitute value (“no request”) or the maximum value is transmitted on the signal.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">In parallel hybrid projects, the transmission transmits the summarized torque request of the combustion engine and the electric machine.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">This signal is defined for an absolute intervention. The interface for relative interventions to the reference "Powertrain: Torque at Clutch without Transmission Intervention" must be defined separately.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">References to other signals:
PtTqCluWoTrsmIntv</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>TrsmTqCluMaxFastReqForShiftIntv</SHORT-NAME>
				  <LONG-NAME>
					<L-4 L="EN">Transmission: Request for Maximum Torque at Clutch for Shift Intervention on Fast Path</L-4>
				  </LONG-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>TrsmTqCluMaxProtnReq1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Transmission: Maximum Torque at Clutch Requested by Transmission for Gearbox Protection</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Maximum torque limitation for gearbox protection.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">A torque decrease in the engine is performed via fast path and slow path.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">The engine limits the value of the torque at clutch as defined in the signal "Powertrain: Torque at Clutch", so the effects of dynamic torque are not considered.
The lower limit to be considered by the engine depends on the torque necessary for the engine internal stall protection.
The global target is to prevent damage to gearbox and drivetrain, e.g. caused by mechanical and thermal overload.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">The indicated torque must be calculated based on this signal, without consideration of the torque influence of inertia. </L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Although this signal is a transmission intervention, the effect must also be visible on all signals with the suffix "...without Intervention".</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">The calculation of this signal by the provider is not permitted to consider the inertia, which has an effect on the torque at clutch. This means that the signal must be calculated as if the inertia is 0 kg*(m^2).</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">References to other signals:
PtTqClu</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>TrsmTqCluMaxProtnReq</SHORT-NAME>
				  <LONG-NAME>
					<L-4 L="EN">Transmission: Maximum Torque at Clutch Requested by Transmission for Gearbox Protection</L-4>
				  </LONG-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME NAME-PATTERN="{anyName}">TrsmTqCluMaxSlowReqForShiftIntv1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Transmission: Request for Maximum Torque at Clutch for Shift Intervention on Slow Path</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Maximum torque at clutch requested by transmission for shift intervention on slow path.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Usually used for shift intervention, but permitted for all purposes.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">As long as there is no torque request from the transmission, a constant substitute value (“no request”) or the maximum value is transmitted on the signal.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">In parallel hybrid projects, the transmission transmits the summarized torque request of the combustion engine and the electric machine.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">This signal is defined for an absolute intervention. The interface for relative interventions to the reference "Powertrain: Torque at Clutch without Transmission Intervention" must be defined separately.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">References to other signals:
PtTqCluWoTrsmIntv</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>TrsmTqCluMaxSlowReqForShiftIntv</SHORT-NAME>
				  <LONG-NAME>
					<L-4 L="EN">Transmission: Request for Maximum Torque at Clutch for Shift Intervention on Slow Path</L-4>
				  </LONG-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME NAME-PATTERN="{anyName}">TrsmTqCluMinFastReqForShiftIntv1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Transmission: Request for Minimum Torque at Clutch for Shift Intervention on Fast Path</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Minimum torque at clutch requested by transmission for shift intervention on fast path.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Usually used for shift intervention, but permitted for all purposes.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">As long as there is no torque request from the transmission, a constant substitute value (“no request”) or the minimum value is transmitted on the signal.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">In parallel hybrid projects, the transmission transmits the summarized torque request of the combustion engine and the electric machine.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">This signal is defined for an absolute intervention. The interface for relative interventions to the reference "Powertrain: Torque at Clutch without Transmission Intervention" must be defined separately.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">References to other signals:
PtTqCluWoTrsmIntv</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>TrsmTqCluMinFastReqForShiftIntv</SHORT-NAME>
				  <LONG-NAME>
					<L-4 L="EN">Transmission: Request for Minimum Torque at Clutch for Shift Intervention on Fast Path</L-4>
				  </LONG-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>TrsmTqCluMinProtnReq1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Transmission: Minimum Torque at Clutch Requested by Transmission for Gearbox Protection</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Minimum torque limitation for gearbox protection.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">The global target is to prevent damage to gearbox and drivetrain, e.g. caused by mechanical and thermal overload. The signal ensures that the gearbox is not loaded with very low negative torque at clutch.
Signal is relevant for projects with an electric machine.
The implementation of the gearbox request is limited by the driving motors:
For efficiency and safety reasons, the minimum torque for gearbox protection is not permitted to lead to a positive indicated or inner torque on any of the driving motors.
The limitation must be implemented only by affecting the negative torque of the electric machine.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">The effects of dynamic torque are not considered.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Although this signal is a transmission intervention, the effect must also be visible on all signals with the suffix "...without Transmission Intervention".</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>TrsmTqCluMinProtnReq</SHORT-NAME>
				  <LONG-NAME>
					<L-4 L="EN">Transmission: Minimum Torque at Clutch Requested by Transmission for Gearbox Protection</L-4>
				  </LONG-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME NAME-PATTERN="{anyName}">TrsmTqCluMinSlowReqForShiftIntv1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Transmission: Request for Minimum Torque at Clutch for Shift Intervention on Slow Path</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Minimum torque at clutch requested by transmission for shift intervention on slow path.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Usually used for shift intervention, but permitted for all purposes.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">As long as there is no torque request from the transmission, a constant substitute value (“no request”) or the minimum value is transmitted on the signal.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">In parallel hybrid projects, the transmission transmits the summarized torque request of the combustion engine and the electric machine.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">This signal is defined for an absolute intervention. The interface for relative interventions to the reference "Powertrain: Torque at Clutch without Transmission Intervention" must be defined separately.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">References to other signals:
PtTqCluWoTrsmIntv</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>TrsmTqCluMinSlowReqForShiftIntv</SHORT-NAME>
				  <LONG-NAME>
					<L-4 L="EN">Transmission: Request for Minimum Torque at Clutch for Shift Intervention on Slow Path</L-4>
				  </LONG-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME NAME-PATTERN="{anyName}">TrsmTqCluReqForShiftIntv1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Transmission: Request for Torque at Clutch for Shift Intervention</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Torque at clutch requested by transmission for shift intervention.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">This signal is closely related to the signals for "implementation type" and “intervention mode” of request:
“Transmission: Implementation Type of Request for Torque at Clutch for Shift Intervention”,
“Transmission: Intervention Mode Request for Torque at Clutch for Shift Intervention”.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Usually used for shift interventions, but permitted for all purposes.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">As long as there is no torque request, the signal "Transmission: Implementation Type of Request for Torque at Clutch for Shift Intervention", is “0h = no request” and signal “Transmission: Request for Torque at Clutch for Shift Intervention” is “FFEh = Init”.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">In parallel hybrid projects, the transmission transmits the summarized torque request of the combustion engine and the electric machine.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">References to other signals:
TrsmNrTypOfTqCluReqForShiftIntv
TrsmIntvModReqForTqCluReqForShiftIntv</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>TrsmTqCluReqForShiftIntv</SHORT-NAME>
				  <LONG-NAME>
					<L-4 L="EN">Transmission: Request for Torque at Clutch for Shift Intervention</L-4>
				  </LONG-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>TrsmTqCluResvReq1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Transmission: Request for Torque Reserve at Clutch</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Request to increase torque on slow path without affecting torque at clutch. Reference for increase is defined by the corresponding status signal.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">This signal is closely related to "Transmission: Implementation Type of Request for Torque Reserve at Clutch".
The engine must compensate for the increased air mass by ignition retard and/or injection cutoff. The engine is not permitted to increase the air mass more than can be compensated for. This prevents unintended acceleration of the car.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">This torque reserve prepares the engine to implement torque increase requests as quickly as it is required.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">References to other signals:
TrsmNrTypOfTqCluResvReq</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>TrsmTqCluResvReq</SHORT-NAME>
				  <LONG-NAME>
					<L-4 L="EN">Transmission: Request for Torque Reserve at Clutch</L-4>
				  </LONG-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>TrsmTqCluStandStillPred1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Transmission: Predicted Transmission Torque at Clutch in Standstill</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Predicted transmission torque at clutch in vehicle motion state “Standstill”.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">Predicted value of torque at clutch consumed by the transmission in standstill. It includes the torque losses caused by the transmission oil pump and the slipping drive-off element such as converter and drive-off clutch. It is calculated continuously, depending on the gear lever position and the targeted state of power transmission.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">The transmission calculates this signal by using the engine speed setpoint.
The signal is to be used as a prediction in the idle speed controller at vehicle standstill.</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>TrsmTqCluStandStillPred</SHORT-NAME>
				  <LONG-NAME>
					<L-4 L="EN">Transmission: Predicted Transmission Torque at Clutch in Standstill</L-4>
				  </LONG-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq5</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
