			  <SHORT-NAME>TrsmTqDftlTrfMax1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Transmission: Maximum Differential Transfer Torque</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Absolute value of the maximum torque at the Transfer Case Differential</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>TrsmTqDftlTrfMax</SHORT-NAME>
				  <DESC>
					<L-2 L="EN">Absolute value of the maximum torque at the Transfer Case Differential</L-2>
				  </DESC>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq14</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>TrsmTqOilPmp1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Transmission: Transmission Oil Pump Load</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Transmission oil pump load at clutch level.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">The torque consumption of the transmission oil pump especially depends on the gearbox temperature, rotational speed and system pressure of the transmission hydraulic system.
Typically, the values are from test bench measurements.
Used to distinguish between gearbox core losses and gearbox oil pump torque losses, which can only be measured together.
The signal can be used by the propulsion unit to calculate Torque at Clutch with higher precision, especially for transmissions with a permanently connected transmission oil pump.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">If the pump is an electric oil pump, then the value should be zero Nm, because the load is included in the alternator load.
The value of this signal is converted to clutch torque by the provider.</L-1>
				  <L-1 L="EN">The value sent on the network is the absolute value of the transmission torque losses.
The value on the application level must consider the sign. The Application Data Type must cover negative values.</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>TrsmTqOilPmp</SHORT-NAME>
				  <LONG-NAME>
					<L-4 L="EN">Transmission: Transmission Oil Pump Load</L-4>
				  </LONG-NAME>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq6</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			<SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
			  <SHORT-NAME>TrsmTqWhlIndDistbn1</SHORT-NAME>
			  <LONG-NAME>
				<L-4 L="EN">Individual Torque at Wheel Distribution as Realized by Transmission System</L-4>
			  </LONG-NAME>
			  <DESC>
				<L-2 L="EN">Individual torque at wheel distribution as realized by Transmission System. Vector of 4 signals.</L-2>
			  </DESC>
			  <INTRODUCTION>
				<P>
				  <L-1 L="EN">The DTD (drivetrain torque distribution) component in the transmission system realizes the torque distribution request and powertrain coordinator sends the coordinated actual wheel torques as feedback to the chassis. This interface only considers the torque which can be distributed from one or more central torque producers to the wheels by the transmission system. It does not consider additional torque producers located e.g. at the individual wheels. Where no torque is distributed to the wheels by the transmission system (e.g. one axle not driven or directly driven by an electric machine), the respective values are zero.
In case of actor/sensor failures or if there is no possibility to determine the correct distribution a rough estimation is done. Additionally a qualifier has to be set, to inform about invalid or backup values.</L-1>
				</P>
			  </INTRODUCTION>
			  <IS-SERVICE>false</IS-SERVICE>
			  <DATA-ELEMENTS>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>TrsmTqWhlIndDistbnFrntLe</SHORT-NAME>
				  <DESC>
					<L-2 L="EN">Front left wheel</L-2>
				  </DESC>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq7</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>TrsmTqWhlIndDistbnFrntRi</SHORT-NAME>
				  <DESC>
					<L-2 L="EN">Front right wheel</L-2>
				  </DESC>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq7</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>TrsmTqWhlIndDistbnReLe</SHORT-NAME>
				  <DESC>
					<L-2 L="EN">Rear left wheel</L-2>
				  </DESC>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq7</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				<VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
				  <SHORT-NAME>TrsmTqWhlIndDistbnReRi</SHORT-NAME>
				  <DESC>
					<L-2 L="EN">Rear right wheel</L-2>
				  </DESC>
				  <TYPE-TREF BASE="ApplicationDataTypes" DEST="APPLICATION-PRIMITIVE-DATA-TYPE">Tq7</TYPE-TREF>
				</VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE>
			  </DATA-ELEMENTS>
			</SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE>
